          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praśikṣaṇa is built on pra- and śikṣaṇa, \"learning; teaching, instruction\" (MW), from śikṣ, the desiderative of √śak, \"to be able\". MW does not list praśikṣaṇa, so the word for training is a modern coinage."
